      "facts": [
        "GitHub is a single action: star the repository. There is no comment to write, so everything comment-shaped (suggestions, comment URLs, the comment paste-back) is skipped for it — see `platformRequiresComment`.",
        "YouTube is a comment under a video. It is only ever bought through the Earn chat as the single `comment` action; the bundle here is the same one step, so a YouTube post with no action set still asks for something sensible.",
        "Platforms bought only through the Earn chat's campaign assistant. The advertiser console's own forms and routes do not take their links: nothing there prices a single action or asks for a verified account.",
        "Normalized, so a pasted `x.com/...` resolves to X rather than to null."
      ],
